Author:     Alessandro Castellani <alessandro@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Fri Oct 4 13:29:05 2024 +0300
Commit:     Alessandro Castellani <alessandro@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 4 13:29:05 2024 +0300

    Bug 1920747 - Ensure the hasNew CSS property is only used when also hasUnread is present. r=Paenglab,micahilbery,vineet


    The "hasNew" style of the reply button should be styled consistently
    in all instances, and clear out immediately after the last new/unread
    message of a thread is touched.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D224549

diff --git a/mail/themes/shared/mail/threadCard.css b/mail/themes/shared/mail/threadCard.css
index 59cc70237f3..3c67dd29fe1 100644
--- a/mail/themes/shared/mail/threadCard.css
+++ b/mail/themes/shared/mail/threadCard.css
@@ -170,23 +170,24 @@
           }
         }
       }
-    }

-    &[data-properties~="hasNew"] {
+      /* hasNew shouldn't affect any style unless we also have hasUnread. */
+      &[data-properties~="hasNew"] {

-      & .replies-icon,
-      & .thread-replies {
-        color: var(--new-color);
-      }
+        & .replies-icon,
+        & .thread-replies {
+          color: var(--new-color);
+        }

-      & button.twisty::before {
-        content: var(--icon-sparkle-star-xs);
-        fill: var(--color-yellow-30);
-        stroke: var(--color-amber-50);
-      }
+        & button.twisty::before {
+          content: var(--icon-sparkle-star-xs);
+          fill: var(--color-yellow-30);
+          stroke: var(--color-amber-50);
+        }

-      & .thread-replies {
-        color: var(--new-color);
+        & .thread-replies {
+          color: var(--new-color);
+        }
       }
     }
